rmal differential is atypical for prolonged viral processes)", "Diabetic complication (hypercalcemia and leukocytosis are not hallmark features of diabetes-related syndromes)", "Hematologic malignancy (considered but hypercalcemia is more specific for paraneoplastic vs CML)", "Hyperparathyroidism (hypercalcemia present but no parathyroid-specific evidence in this timepoint)"], "alarm_features": ["Weight loss", "Hypercalcemia", "Leukocytosis with elevated LALP"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.02, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of blasts in the peripheral smear (normal differential) contradicts the diagnosis of myeloid neoplasm with increased blasts."]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.059802158273381284, "posterior": 0.09862427465499861, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Constitutional symptoms and hypercalcemia are not features of reactive leukocytosis, which is typically associated with benign causes."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.39469424460431646, "posterior": 0.6509202127229905, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Constitutional symptoms and hypercalcemia are not features of reactive leukocytosis, which is typically associated with benign causes."], "e