rential is atypical for prolonged viral processes)", "Diabetic complication (hypercalcemia and leukocytosis are not hallmark features of diabetes-related syndromes)", "Hematologic malignancy (considered but hypercalcemia is more specific for paraneoplastic vs CML)", "Hyperparathyroidism (hypercalcemia present but no parathyroid-specific evidence in this timepoint)"], "alarm_features": ["Weight loss", "Hypercalcemia", "Leukocytosis with elevated LALP"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of blasts in the peripheral smear (normal differential) contradicts the diagnosis of myeloid neoplasm with increased blasts."]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.09862427465499861, "posterior": 0.041860644524676166, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Constitutional symptoms and hypercalcemia are not features of reactive leukocytosis, which is typically associated with benign causes."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.6509202127229905, "posterior": 0.35535298721072045, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Constitutional symptoms and hypercalcemia are not features of reactive leukocytosis, which is typically associated with benign causes."], "evidence_against": ["Elevated LALP is atypical for chronic myeloid leukemia, which typically presents with low LALP. This weakens CML as a candidate."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3", "B3.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.65, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.164, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The normal differential contradicts lymphoid neoplasms, which often present with lymphocytosis or atypical lymphocytes."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.011, "danger": 0.4, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Constitutional symptoms and hypercalcemia are not features of reactive leukocytosis, which is typically associated with benign causes."]}, "B2.1": {"id": "B2.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL)", "parent": "B2", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.049312137327499304, "posterior": 0.019172618154836753, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Hypercalcemia is atypical for PMF but more suggestive of aggressive lymphoid processes. Constitutional symptoms are non-specific but may raise concern for mali…"], "evidence_against": ["Subacute presentation is more consistent with chronic myeloid processes (e.g., PMF) than acute lymphoblastic leukemia, which typically has abrupt onset."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_